# Build context exclusions for the ROOT-context image build
# (`docker build -f kates/Dockerfile .`, used by `make kates-image-local` and
# the publish workflow).
#
# kates/.dockerignore does NOT apply here — Docker reads the one at the context
# root — so without this file the whole repository is uploaded to the daemon on
# every build: the git history, the vendored Strimzi operator, and hundreds of
# megabytes of previous build output. `COPY cli/ ./` would then also drag
# prebuilt CLI binaries into the Go builder stage, where they shadow nothing but
# cost time on every layer.
#
# Everything the Dockerfile actually needs is kates/pom.xml, kates/.mvn,
# kates/mvnw, kates/src and cli/ sources.

# Version control and CI
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitmodules

# Build output
**/target/
cli/dist/
cli/bin/
cli/.build/
bin/
build/

# Vendored upstream chart source — never part of the image
strimzi-kafka-operator/

# Charts, scenarios and scripts are deployment-time assets, not build inputs
charts/
scenarios/
scripts/
config/
proxy/
tester/

# Docs and notes
docs/
**/*.md
!README.md

# Local artefacts
*.log
*.tgz
.idea/
.vscode/
.metals/
.bsp/
**/*.iml
